    "summary": "In <b>Spelling</b> questions SSC gives four words and asks you to pick the <b>correctly spelt</b> one (or sometimes the misspelt one). The words tested are commonly confused ones with double letters, silent letters or <i>-ance/-ence</i> endings.",
    "concepts": [
      { "title": "Double letters", "body": "Most errors are about how many letters repeat. Learn the tricky ones: <i>accommodate</i> (cc, mm), <i>committee</i> (mm, tt, ee), <i>embarrass</i> (rr, ss), <i>occurrence</i> (cc, rr), <i>necessary</i> (one c, ss)." },
      { "title": "Common patterns", "body": "<ul><li><b>i before e except after c</b>: <i>believe, receive</i> (exceptions: <i>seize, weird</i>).</li><li><b>Drop the silent e</b> before <i>-ing</i>: <i>write → writing</i>; but keep it in <i>noticeable, manageable</i>.</li><li><b>-ance / -ence</b>: <i>maintenance, guidance</i> vs <i>existence, independence</i>.</li></ul>" }
    ],
